  "articleBody": "If your bathroom walls are soft to the touch, showing peeling paint, or carrying recurring stains, you're likely facing water damage behind the surface. Before you sign a repair contract, it's critical to know whether your contractor treats the underlying cause or just plasters over the symptom. \n\nQuestions to Ask Before You Decide:\n- Will you identify and stop the moisture leak first? Cosmetic fixes fail fast if an active pipe leak or failing grout continues to soak the wall cavity.\n- Do you verify framing is completely dry before hanging new board? EPA guidelines stress drying wet materials promptly—within 24 to 48 hours—to prevent mold growth. Enclosing damp cavities traps rot.\n- What board are you installing? Standard gypsum won't hold up in wet zones; moisture-resistant panels or cement backer boards should protect shower areas.\n- How will you blend the finish? Seamless tape embedding, sanding, and proper priming keep repairs invisible once painted.\n\nWhen extensive mold appears, insulation gets soaked, or electrical wiring runs near the leak, bringing in an experienced team protects your home. At HH Remodeling LLC, owner Abraham Becerra handles hands-on drywall installation, repairs, and full bathroom renovations across the Denver metro area. Give us a call at 303-505-0866 or message us online to discuss your project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
